  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinnligt ledarskap  och medborgarinflytande p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; IDEA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women Leadership and CItizen Participation  at the Local Level IDEA - Kvinnligt ledarskap p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bidraget syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kvaliteten av kvinnors politiska deltagande i de nio nyligen bildade bolivianska autonoma regeringarna. Kvinnliga ledare som arbetar i de regionala regeringarna kommer att f&#xe5; s&#xe4;rskild teknisk assistans f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka sina personliga f&#xe4;rdigheter f&#xf6;r att ytterligare f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra sina beslutsprocesser.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDEA has applied to Sida for a funding of 19 million SEK to carry out the &quot;Women leadership and Citizen participation at local level&quot; in the nine Bolivian departments/regions, during the period October 2016 - March 2019.
  
This proposed initiative is aimed to improve the quality of women&#x2019;s political participation in the nine departmental governments, so they will contribute with a more accountable, efficient and solid public management in their respective local governments.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention was intended to provide the beneficiaries, mainlywomen and the youth, with technical assistance to improve their personal skills and to increase the quality of their political participation in the design, promotion and implementation of public policies in their respective regions.&#xa0;
The intervention had the following four outcome objectives:
1. A more efficient and improved public management at regional levels, including higher citizen participation, in the targeted Bolivian regions has been achieved.
2. Women working in the regional governments promote public policies in their respective areas of work.&#xa0;
3. Construction and implementation of the &quot;agenda from the young people&quot; in the targeted regions of the country.&#xa0;
4. The Bolivian Electoral Body obtains the international certification ISO 9000 as a proof of an improved and trustable management system.</narrative>
  </description>
